<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf Frederick, King of Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1710–1771</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf Frederick, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, was a prince of the house of Holstein-Gottorp who served as prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> from 1727 to 1750. Chosen heir to the Swedish throne in 1743 under Russian pressure, he became king in 1751. His reign fell in Sweden's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-liberty">Age of Liberty</a>, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riksdag">Riksdag</a> held real power, and his attempts to strengthen the crown failed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolf-frederick-king-of-sweden.jpg" alt="Adolf Frederick, King of Sweden" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gustaf Lundberg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustaf_Lundberg_-_Portrait_of_Adolf_Frederick,_King_of_Sweden_-_WGA13779.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
